---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import DocsPreview from "../../../components/DocsPreview.astro";
import DocsSidebar from "../../../components/DocsSidebar.astro";
import DocsTOC from "../../../components/DocsTOC.astro";
import DocsPagination from "../../../components/DocsPagination.astro";
import CodeWindow from "../../../components/CodeWindow.astro";
import "../../../styles/docs.css";
---

<Layout title="Typewriter Hero — Recipes — Motion Components" description="A hero section with a character-by-character typewriter headline and a fading subcopy. The typewriter adds presence, the reveal adds depth." noMain>
  <div class="layout">
    <DocsSidebar />

    <main id="main">
      <h1>Typewriter Hero</h1>
      <p class="lead">A hero section with a character-by-character typewriter headline and a fading subcopy. The typewriter adds presence, the reveal adds depth.</p>

      <h2>Preview</h2>
      <DocsPreview wide>
        <div class="hero-demo">
          <p class="hero-headline">
            <motion-typewriter interval="0.04" delay="0.3" cursor>Build interactions that ship.</motion-typewriter>
          </p>
          <motion-reveal y="16" duration="0.6" delay="0.2">
            <p class="hero-sub">Physics-based web components for any framework. No easing curves to tune.</p>
          </motion-reveal>
        </div>
      </DocsPreview>

      <h2>Complete code</h2>
      <CodeWindow
        filename="typewriter-hero.html"
        copy
        code={`<section class="hero">
  <h1>
    <motion-typewriter interval="0.04" delay="0.3" cursor>Build interactions that ship.</motion-typewriter>
  </h1>

  <motion-reveal y="16" duration="0.6">
    <p>Physics-based web components for any framework.
       No easing curves to tune.</p>
  </motion-reveal>
</section>`}
      />

      <h2>How it works</h2>

      <h3>Typewriter headline</h3>
      <CodeWindow
        filename="typewriter.html"
        copy
        compact
        code={`<h1>
  <motion-typewriter interval="0.04" delay="0.3" cursor>Build interactions that ship.</motion-typewriter>
</h1>`}
      />
      <p class="section-lead">The typewriter reveals the headline one character at a time. <code>interval</code> is the time between characters in seconds. <code>delay</code> adds a pause, in seconds, before typing starts. The <code>cursor</code> attribute adds a blinking caret.</p>

      <h3>Reveal subcopy</h3>
      <CodeWindow
        filename="reveal.html"
        copy
        compact
        code={`<motion-reveal y="16" duration="0.6">
  <p>Physics-based web components.</p>
</motion-reveal>`}
      />
      <p class="section-lead">The subcopy fades in with a slight lift. Without an explicit <code>delay</code>, it starts immediately when the element enters the viewport. The different durations create a natural choreography: the typewriter takes longer, the reveal resolves faster.</p>

      <h2>Variations</h2>

      <h3>Looping</h3>
      <CodeWindow
        filename="loop.html"
        copy
        compact
        code={`<h1>
  <motion-typewriter interval="0.04" delay="2" loop cursor>Build. Ship. Iterate.</motion-typewriter>
</h1>`}
      />
      <p class="section-lead">Add <code>loop</code> to cycle through: type, pause, erase, retype. The <code>delay</code> is the pause between cycles in milliseconds.</p>

      <h3>Word-by-word</h3>
      <p class="section-lead">For a calmer, more editorial feel, use <code>motion-headline</code> instead. It reveals word by word with a mask slide rather than character by character.</p>
      <CodeWindow
        filename="headline.html"
        copy
        compact
        code={`<h1>
  <motion-headline by="words" interval="0.06" duration="1">The future of motion</motion-headline>
</h1>`}
      />

      <h2>Accessibility</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">The typewriter respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>: the full text appears instantly with no character-by-character animation, and the caret does not blink. Screen readers always read the full text, even while it types. Put the typewriter inside the <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>, not around it: it replaces its own content, so a heading inside it would be lost.</p>

      <DocsPagination />
    </main>
    <DocsTOC />
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import "motion-components/motion-reveal";
  import "motion-components/motion-typewriter";
</script>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .lead {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .section-lead {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .section-lead code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-accent-dim);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .hero-demo {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 2rem 3rem;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .hero-headline {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
